/*
    One whole Pfam-A.hmm for the nail arms, in place of Codon's 20 chunks.

    nail searches one HMM file, so a chunked Pfam means one seeding task per chunk, and each
    rebuilds its MMseqs2 query database over the sample's whole ORF set. B11 measured 20 tasks
    of about 1.5 minutes per sample, nearly all of it that repeated setup. One task searching
    the whole database does the same work once.

    run.sh exports PFAM_HMM_DIR, PFAM_HMM_NAME and PFAM_NUM_MODELS, the last counted from the
    file so `-Z` matches the hmmsearch arms. Pass this config to the nail arms only: the
    hmmsearch arms want the chunks, which are how they parallelise.

    `chunked: false` matters. Assigning this map merges it into what the site config already set,
    so the per-chunk entries stay behind; the pipeline reads them only when `chunked` is true.
*/
params.databases.pfam = [
    chunked: false,
    remote_path: '',
    remote_checksum_path: false,
    remote_checksum: false,
    local_path: System.getenv('PFAM_HMM_DIR') ?: '',
    files: [hmm: System.getenv('PFAM_HMM_NAME') ?: 'Pfam-A.hmm'],
    variables: [num_models: (System.getenv('PFAM_NUM_MODELS') ?: '0').toInteger()],
]
